# Keep line endings consistent across clones.
#
# Without this file, text normalization is decided by each machine's
# core.autocrlf setting. On Windows that meant the working copy used CRLF while
# the repository stored LF, so every changed line showed up as trailing
# whitespace in `git diff --check` and two clones could disagree about a file.
#
# Settings here take precedence over core.autocrlf, so behaviour no longer
# depends on how a contributor has git configured.
* text=auto

# Binary assets: never line-ending normalized, and never diffed.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
